# The history viewer previews a moon's history on the selection screen, before the moon is taken,
# and what it previews is the history the run then gets.
#
# The window itself is not checked here (it is a WinForms window, and the suite runs --hidden); what
# is checked is what feeds it. The preview is built headless and off the main thread, from the moon's
# seed alone, so the one thing that could go wrong silently is that it describes a different past
# from the one the game generates on CONFIRM. `preview=match` on the world-history line is the game
# comparing the two hashes itself.
#
# Runs without --seed, like world_selection.cli, because the flag skips the selection screen.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --no-encounters --silent --no-save --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode WorldSelection 20
expect-state world-preview none

# Choosing a moon starts its preview; `wait` outlasts the build.
click moon Prunil
wait
expect-state world-preview Prunil
expect-state world-preview state=ready

# Changing one's mind previews the new moon instead.
click moon Belune
wait
expect-state world-preview state=ready
expect-no-state world-preview Prunil

click world confirm
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

expect-state world-history Belune
expect-state world-history preview=match

quit
